<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you have looked into local SEO, you will have met the word "citation" and the letters NAP. Both are simpler than they sound, and getting them right is one of the cheapest ways to help a local business appear on Google Maps.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">What a citation is</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A citation is a mention of your business details on another website: a directory such as Yell, a map service such as Apple Maps or Bing Places, a review site, a trade body or a local chamber of commerce. It usually includes your name, address and phone number, and often your website, opening hours and a description.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">What NAP means</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>NAP stands for name, address and phone number. "NAP consistency" means those three things appear in exactly the same form wherever your business is listed.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Why consistency matters</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Google wants to show businesses that really exist, at the address and phone number shown. It checks your Google Business Profile against what it finds elsewhere. When everything matches, it can be confident. When one site has your old phone number and another has a different spelling of your name, it has less reason to trust any of them.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It matters to customers too. An old number on a directory is a lost call.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">What counts as inconsistent</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>An old address or phone number after a move.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Different versions of the name: "Smith Plumbing", "Smith Plumbing Ltd", "Smiths Plumbers".</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>A mobile number in one place and a landline in another.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>A tracking phone number used on some listings.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Duplicate listings for the same business on one site.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Small formatting differences, such as "Street" and "St", are not worth worrying about. Different numbers, names and addresses are.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

